//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * @page c_tafecall Emergency Call Service
 *
 * @ref taf_ecall_interface.h "API Reference"
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 * eCall is a technology initiative intended to bring rapid assistance to auto accidents anywhere.
 * When a serious vehicle accident occurs, sensors automatically trigger an eCall.
 * When activated, the in-vehicle system (IVS) establishes a voice connection to Public Safety
 * Answering Point (PSAP). At the same time, a digital "minimum set of data" (MSD) message is sent
 * over the voice call using in-band modem signals. The MSD includes accident information like
 * time, location, driving direction, and vehicle description.
 * The eCall can also be triggered manually.
 * An emergency call is needed for applications that want to establish an emergency communication
 * with a remote party. The emergency call can be over an emergency mobile network, or over VoIP.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_binding IPC interfaces binding
 *
 * All these functions of the API are provided by @b tafECallSvc application service.
 * TafECallSvc allows to start an ecall, talk/conversation through ecall, send MSD information.
 * It also allows to send location info to Public Safety Answering Point (PSAP).
 *
 * Here's a sample of how to bind to Emergency Call services:
 * @verbatim
   bindings:
   {
       clientExe.clientComponent.taf_ecall -> tafECallSvc.taf_ecall
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_operation Operation modes of eCall
 *
 * The modem is capable to operate in three different eCall operation modes:
 * - taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode(): This API makes the eCall operating mode to eCall only, in this mode,
 *   to start an eCall session only emergency number should be used. The modem may not try to register
 *   in the Cellular network. The modem is forced to behave as only eCall allow mode by this function
 *   whatever the U/SIM operation mode. The change is not persistent if device reboot.
 *   So this function may need to be called before start an eCall.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_ForcePersistentOnlyMode(): Same as taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode(), but this change persists
 *   over device restart i.e. power cycles.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_ExitOnlyMode(): This function comes out from eCall Only mode. It changes the eCall
 *   operation mode to Normal. Generally modem applies default operation mode at boot up (and
 *   after U/SIM hotswap). The modem acts following the U/SIM eCall operation mode. For example the
 *   U/SIM can be setup only for eCall, or a combination of the eCall and also normal commercial
 *   service provision.
 *
 * - taf_ecall_GetConfiguredOperationMode(): This function helps the user to fetch configured
 *   Operation mode in modem or NAD.
 *   The various operation modes can be:
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_MODE_NORMAL : It's normal mode. The modem acts as the U/SIM eCall operation
 *                                  mode.
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_MODE_ECALL : eCall only mode as per U/SIM operation mode or forced by
 *                                 the application through taf_ecall_ForceOnlyMode() API.
 *   - @ref TAF_ECALL_FORCED_PERSISTENT_ONLY_MODE : It's eCall only mode and persistent over power cycles.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_session Session of eCall
 *
 * taf_ecall_Create() helps to create a new eCall object and it returns a reference of eCall session.
 * At this point the eCall is not yet started, the eCall session must be started using one of the
 * below functions:
 * - taf_ecall_StartManual(): To initiate a manual eCall session (triggered by a passenger)
 * - taf_ecall_StartAutomatic(): It initiates an automatic eCall session which triggered automatically
 *   by the IVS if there is an accident or emrgency.
 * - taf_ecall_StartTest(): It initiates a test eCall session (mainly to test the communication between
 *   the IVS and the PSAP)
 *
 * The eCall session can be ended by calling taf_ecall_End(). Note that sometimes, the ongoing eCall
 * session cannot be stopped until a specific eCall state is arrived. Such cases are as below:
 * - When an automatic eCall session is in progress, it is not possible to stop the ongoing session
 *   until @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED event is reached.
 * - For manual session, it is allowed to end the ongoing session if eCall is not connected/active
 *   (@ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ACTIVE not yet come) and after @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED event is received.
 *
 * @warning An application should wait for end of the existing eCall before dialing another
 * one with the @c taf_ecall_StartXxx() APIs. An eCall is stopped when:
 * - the application successfully stops it with taf_ecall_End() returning @c LE_OK
 * - or the event @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED arrives
 * - or the event @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_CLEAR_DOWN is notified
 * - or the event @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_FAILED is notified and no redial is initiated.
 *
 * If the eCall object is no more required, application can call taf_ecall_Delete() to free
 * all allocated resources of the eCall object.
 *
 * The current state of the eCall session may be queried by taf_ecall_GetState().
 * Apart from this, an application may register a state change handler to get notified when the
 * session state changes. The handler can be controlled using taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler()
 * and taf_ecall_RemoveStateChangeHandler().
 *
 * An application may also call taf_ecall_GetTerminationReason() to get end reason of the eCall
 * when eCall state is @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_ENDED, and also
 * taf_ecall_GetPlatformSpecificTerminationCode() to get platform related termination code.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_concurrency Concurrency of eCall
 *
 * If other application wants to use the eCall service when a session is already in active, the
 * taf_ecall_StartManual(), taf_ecall_StartAutomatic(), taf_ecall_StartTest() functions will return
 * @ref LE_BUSY error and the eCall session which is in progress won't be interrupted or disturbed.
 * The application may get the session progress 'state' using API like @ref taf_ecall_GetState() and
 * @ref taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler().
 * Another point is, a manual eCall can't disturb an automatic eCall and vice-versa.
 *
 * @section taf_ecall_msd Minimum Set of Data (MSD)
 *
 * The dynamic values of MSD can be written with:
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPosition() : It sets position of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPositionN1() : It sets first delta position of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPositionN2() : It sets second delta position of the vehicle.
 * - taf_ecall_SetMsdPassengersCount() : It sets the number of passengers.
 *
 * The MSD is automatically encoded with the previous MSD values set earlier.
 *
 * @warning Above functions may return a @ref LE_DUPLICATE error when MSD has been already imported
 * using taf_ecall_ImportMsd() API.
 *
 * The MSD transmission mode can be set and got using below API:
 *  - taf_ecall_SetMsdTxMode()
 *  - taf_ecall_GetMsdTxMode()
 *
 * The transmission modes can be as follows:
 * - @ref TAF_ECALL_TX_MODE_PUSH : The MSD has been pushed by the IVS
 * - @ref TAF_ECALL_TX_MODE_PULL : The MSD has been sent when asked by the PSAP
 *
 * An application can import an existing MSD using the taf_ecall_ImportMsd() API.
 * The existing MSD must follow requirements presented in the "EN 15722:2013" publication (this
 * publication is prepared by Technical Committee CEN/TC 278 “Intelligent Transport Systems").
 *
 * @warning The imported MSD doesn't consider the values provided by the
 * taf_ecall_SetMsdXxx() APIs. It overwrites any MSD imported or encoded previously.
 *
 * @warning The imported MSD may overwrite the control flags (automatic and test eCall) set by
 * taf_ecall_StartXxx() APIs (Manual, Automatic, Test). The user App is responsible for the
 * proper settings.
 *
 * The encoded MSD can be fetched with taf_ecall_ExportMsd() API.
 *
 * @note The user application should perform the MSD transmission by using taf_ecall_SendMsd() when the
 * @ref TAF_ECALL_STATE_PSAP_START_RECEIVED event arrives.
 * The MSD may be modified before calling taf_ecall_SendMsd() by the e_ecall_ImportMsd() API
 * or the taf_ecall_SetMsdXxx() APIs.
 *
 * @section c_taf_ecall_outgoing Start of emergency call
 *
 * An emergency call can be started by using taf_ecall_StartAutomatic() with the ecallRef passed as
 * parameter.
 * To get ECallRef we need to call taf_ecall_Create() with no parameter. This function will create
 * an ECallRef object and return it. App can cache the ECallRef for future usages.
 * @verbatim
   static taf_ecall_CallRef_t ECallRef = taf_ecall_Create();
   if (!ECallRef)
   {
      le_result_t res = taf_ecall_StartAutomatic(ECallRef);
      LE_ASSERT(res == LE_OK);
   }
   @endverbatim
 *
 * Before the emergency call is started, an application registers a state change handler using
 * taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler(). Once the emergency call is established, the handler will be
 * called indicating it's now connected. If the state of the emergency call changes, then the
 * handler will be called with the new state.
 * @verbatim
   taf_ecall_StateChangeHandlerRef = taf_ecall_AddStateChangeHandler((taf_ecall_StateChangeHandlerFunc_t) tafECallStateHandler, NULL);
   @endverbatim
 *
 * To stop an emergency call, an application can use taf_ecall_End().
 *
 * Application must use taf_ecall_Delete() to release @ref taf_ecall_CallRef_t emergency call
 * reference object when it is no more used.
 *
 * <HR>
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


USETYPES taf_sim.api;
REFERENCE Call;

/**
 * To support legacy opmode
 */
DEFINE NORMAL_MODE = 0;
DEFINE FORCED_PERSISTENT_ONLY_MODE = 1;
DEFINE ONLY_MODE = 3;
DEFINE TX_MODE_PULL = 0;
DEFINE TX_MODE_PUSH = 1;

DEFINE MAX_VIN_LENGTH  =  (17);
DEFINE MAX_VIN_BYTES  =  MAX_VIN_LENGTH + (1);
DEFINE  MAX_MSD_LENGTH = (140);

/**
 *  Represents an operational mode
 */
ENUM OpMode
{
    MODE_NORMAL,           ///< eCall and normal voice calls are allowed
    MODE_ECALL,            ///< Only eCall is allowed.
    NONE                   ///< Invalid mode
};

/**
 *  Represents MSD transmission mode as per eCall MSD standard
 */
ENUM MsdTransmissionMode
{
    MSD_TX_MODE_PULL,  ///< Pull mode (modem/host waits for MSD request from PSAP to send MSD).
    MSD_TX_MODE_PUSH   ///< Push mode (modem/host sends MSD to PSAP right after eCall connected).
};

/**
 *  Represents a vehicle class as per European eCall MSD standard.
 *
 */
ENUM MsdVehicleType
{
    PASSENGER_VEHICLE_CLASS_M1,            ///< Passenger vehicle (Class M1)
    BUSES_AND_COACHES_CLASS_M2,            ///< Passenger vehicle (Class M1)
    BUSES_AND_COACHES_CLASS_M3,            ///< Buses and coaches (Class M3)
    LIGHT_COMMERCIAL_VEHICLES_CLASS_N1,    ///< Light commercial vehicles (Class N1)
    HEAVY_DUTY_VEHICLES_CLASS_N2,          ///< Heavy duty vehicles (Class N2)
    HEAVY_DUTY_VEHICLES_CLASS_N3,          ///< Heavy duty vehicles (Class N3)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L1E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L1e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L2E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L2e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L3E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L3e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L4E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L4e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L5E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L5e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L6E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L6e)
    MOTOR_CYCLES_CLASS_L7E,                ///< Motorcycles (Class L7e)
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Propulsion type Bit Mask
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BITMASK PropulsionStorageType
{
    PROP_TYPE_GASOLINE_TANK,         ///< Represents the presence of Gasoline Tank in the vehicle.
    PROP_TYPE_DIESEL_TANK,           ///< Represents the presence of Diesel Tank in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_COMPRESSED_NATURALGAS, ///< Represents the presence of CNG in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_PROPANE_GAS,           ///< Represents the presence of Liquid Propane Gas in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_ELECTRIC,              ///< Represents the presence of Electronic Storage in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_HYDROGEN,              ///< Represents the presence of Hydrogen Storage in the vehicle
    PROP_TYPE_OTHER,                 ///< Represents the presence of Other types of storage in the vehicle
};

/**
 *  Represents states of the eCall
 *
 */
ENUM State
{
    STATE_UNKNOWN,                            ///< Unknown eCall state
    STATE_ALERTING,                           ///< Alerting call, MO Call only
    STATE_ACTIVE,                             ///< Active eCall
    STATE_IDLE,                               ///< Idle
    STATE_WAITING_PSAP_START_IND,             ///< Not supported
    STATE_PSAP_START_RECEIVED,                ///< SEND-MSD(START) is received and SYNC is locked during in-band MSD transmission
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_STARTED,           ///< In-band MSD transmission started
    STATE_LLNACK_RECEIVED,                    ///< Not supported
    STATE_LL_ACK_RECEIVED,                    ///< Link-Layer Acknowledgement(LL-ACK) is received during in-band MSD transmission
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_SUCCESS,           ///< In-band MSD transmission is successful
    STATE_MSD_TRANSMISSION_FAILED,            ///< In-band MSD transmission failed
    STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_POSITIVE,            ///< Not supported
    STATE_ALACK_RECEIVED_CLEAR_DOWN,          ///< Not supported
    STATE_ENDED,                              ///< Call stopped.
    STATE_RESET,                              ///< Not supported
    STATE_COMPLETED,                          ///< Not supported
    STATE_FAILED,                             ///< eCall start failed.
    STATE_END_OF_REDIAL_PERIOD,               ///< Not supported
    STATE_T2_EXPIRED,                         ///< T2 Timer expired
    STATE_TIMEOUT_T3,                         ///< Not  supported.
    STATE_T5_EXPIRED,                         ///< T5 Timer expired
    STATE_T6_EXPIRED,                         ///< T6 Timer expired
    STATE_T7_EXPIRED,                         ///< T7 Timer expired
    STATE_T9_EXPIRED,                         ///< T9 Timer expired
    STATE_T10_EXPIRED,                        ///< T10 Timer expired
    STATE_DIALING,                            ///< Outgoing call
    STATE_NACK_OUT_OF_ORDER,                  ///< Out of order NACK message detected during in-band MSD transmission
    STATE_ACK_OUT_OF_ORDER,                   ///< Out of order ACK message detected during in-band MSD transmission
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_STARTED,   ///< Outband MSD transmission started in NG eCall
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_SUCCESS,   ///< Outband MSD transmission succeeded in NG eCall
    STATE_OUTBAND_MSD_TRANSMISSION_FAILURE    ///< Outband MSD transmission failed in NG eCall
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Reason for the recently terminated call (either normally ended or failed)
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ENUM TerminationReason
{
   REASON_UNOBTAINABLE_NUMBER = 1,
   REASON_NO_ROUTE_TO_DESTINATION = 3,
   REASON_CHANNEL_UNACCEPTABLE = 6,
   REASON_OPERATOR_DETERMINED_BARRING = 8,
   REASON_NORMAL = 16,
   REASON_BUSY = 17,
   REASON_NO_USER_RESPONDING = 18,
   REASON_NO_ANSWER_FROM_USER = 19,
   REASON_NOT_REACHABLE = 20,
   REASON_CALL_REJECTED = 21,
   REASON_NUMBER_CHANGED = 22,
   REASON_PREEMPTION = 25,
   REASON_DESTINATION_OUT_OF_ORDER = 27,
   REASON_INVALID_NUMBER_FORMAT = 28,
   REASON_FACILITY_REJECTED = 29,
   REASON_RESP_TO_STATUS_ENQUIRY = 30,
   REASON_NORMAL_UNSPECIFIED = 31,
   REASON_CONGESTION = 34,
   REASON_NETWORK_OUT_OF_ORDER = 38,
   REASON_TEMPORARY_FAILURE = 41,
   REASON_SWITCHING_EQUIPMENT_CONGESTION = 42,
   REASON_ACCESS_INFORMATION_DISCARDED = 43,
   REASON_REQUESTED_CIRCUIT_OR_CHANNEL_NOT_AVAILABLE = 44,
   REASON_RESOURCES_UNAVAILABLE_OR_UNSPECIFIED = 47,
   REASON_QOS_UNAVAILABLE = 49,
   REASON_REQUESTED_FACILITY_NOT_SUBSCRIBED = 50,
   REASON_INCOMING_CALLS_BARRED_WITHIN_CUG = 55,
   REASON_BEARER_CAPABILITY_NOT_AUTHORIZED = 57,
   REASON_BEARER_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE = 58,
   REASON_SERVICE_OPTION_NOT_AVAILABLE = 63,
   REASON_BEARER_SERVICE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 65,
   REASON_ACM_LIMIT_EXCEEDED = 68,
   REASON_REQUESTED_FACILITY_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 69,
   REASON_ONLY_DIGITAL_INFORMATION_BEARER_AVAILABLE = 70,
   REASON_SERVICE_OR_OPTION_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = 79,
   REASON_INVALID_TRANSACTION_IDENTIFIER = 81,
   REASON_USER_NOT_MEMBER_OF_CUG = 87,
   REASON_INCOMPATIBLE_DESTINATION = 88,
   REASON_INVALID_TRANSIT_NW_SELECTION = 91,
   REASON_SEMANTICALLY_INCORRECT_MESSAGE = 95,
   REASON_INVALID_MANDATORY_INFORMATION = 96,
   REASON_MESSAGE_TYPE_NON_IMPLEMENTED = 97,
   REASON_MESSAGE_TYPE_NOT_COMPATIBLE_WITH_PROTOCOL_STATE = 98,
   REASON_INFORMATION_ELEMENT_NON_EXISTENT = 99,
   REASON_CONDITIONAL_IE_ERROR = 100,
   REASON_MESSAGE_NOT_COMPATIBLE_WITH_PROTOCOL_STATE = 101,
   REASON_RECOVERY_ON_TIMER_EXPIRED = 102,
   REASON_PROTOCOL_ERROR_UNSPECIFIED = 111,
   REASON_INTERWORKING_UNSPECIFIED = 127,
   REASON_CALL_BARRED = 240,
   REASON_FDN_BLOCKED = 241,
   REASON_IMSI_UNKNOWN_IN_VLR = 242,
   REASON_IMEI_NOT_ACCEPTED = 243,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_USSD = 244,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_SS = 245,
   REASON_DIAL_MODIFIED_TO_DIAL = 246,
   REASON_CDMA_LOCKED_UNTIL_POWER_CYCLE = 1000,
   REASON_CDMA_DROP = 1001,
   REASON_CDMA_INTERCEPT = 1002,
   REASON_CDMA_REORDER = 1003,
   REASON_CDMA_SO_REJECT = 1004,
   REASON_CDMA_RETRY_ORDER = 1005,
   REASON_CDMA_ACCESS_FAILURE = 1006,
   REASON_CDMA_PREEMPTED = 1007,
   REASON_CDMA_NOT_EMERGENCY = 1008,
   REASON_CDMA_ACCESS_BLOCKED = 1009,
   REASON_ERROR_UNSPECIFIED = 0xffff
};

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Handler for changes in eCall state
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
HANDLER StateChangeHandler
(
    Call  ecallRef IN,    ///< Emergency call reference
    State state    IN     ///< Emergency call state
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Events of eCall state changes
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EVENT StateChange
(
    StateChangeHandler handler ///< State change handler of Emergency call
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Create eCall reference
 *
 * @return
 *      - Reference to the emergency call
 *      - NULL if the emergency call can not be created
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION Call Create
(
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Call to free up a call reference according to given ecall reference.
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION Delete
(
    Call ecallRef IN   ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Switch to mode in which only eCall is allowed according to given slot id.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ForceOnlyMode
(
    taf_sim.Id         slotId  IN                  ///< SIM slot id
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Switch to mode in which only eCall is allowed according to given slot id.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ForcePersistentOnlyMode
(
    taf_sim.Id         slotId  IN                  ///< SIM slot id
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Exits from ECALL mode and switch to NORMAL mode according to given slot id.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ExitOnlyMode
(
    taf_sim.Id         slotId  IN                 ///< SIM slot id
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Get the ecall operating mode according to given slot id.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetConfiguredOperationMode
(
    taf_sim.Id         slotId  IN,     ///< SIM slot id
    OpMode             opMode  OUT     ///< Operating mode
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set MSD version.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdVersion
(
    uint32 msdVersion IN
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Get MSD version.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetMsdVersion
(
    uint32 msdVer OUT    ///< MSD version as output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set vehicle type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetVehicleType
(
    MsdVehicleType vehType   IN     ///< Vehicle type
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Get vehicle type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetVehicleType
(
    MsdVehicleType vehType   OUT  ///< Vehicle type as output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set vehicle Identification Number.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetVIN
(
    string vin[MAX_VIN_LENGTH] IN    ///< Vehicle Identification Number
);

/**
 *  Get vehicle Identification Number.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
FUNCTION le_result_t GetVIN
(
    string vin[MAX_VIN_BYTES]  OUT    ///< Vehicle Identification Number as output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set vehicle propulsion storage type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetPropulsionType
(
    PropulsionStorageType propulsionType IN    ///< Vehicle propulsion storage
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Read vehicle propulsion storage type.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetPropulsionType
(
    PropulsionStorageType propulsionType OUT    ///< Vehicle propulsion storage as output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set MSD transmission mode.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdTxMode
(
    MsdTransmissionMode mode IN    ///< MSD transmission mode
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Read MSD transmission mode.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t GetMsdTxMode
(
    MsdTransmissionMode mode OUT    ///< MSD transmission mode as output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set the latitude and longitude for MSD transmission.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdPosition
(
    Call  ecallRef   IN,   ///< SIM slot id
    bool  isTrusted  IN,   ///< Is trusted or not
    int32 latitude   IN,   ///< Latitude value
    int32 longitude  IN,   ///< Longitude value
    int32 direction  IN    ///< Direction
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the change in latitude and longitude compared
 * to the last MSD transmission.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdPositionN1
(
    Call  ecallRef   IN,        ///< SIM slot id
    int32 latitudeDeltaN1 IN,   ///< First Latitude delta
    int32 longitudeDeltaN1 IN   ///< First Longitude delta
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Set the change in latitude and longitude compared
 * to the last MSD transmission.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdPositionN2
(
    Call  ecallRef   IN,        ///< SIM slot id
    int32 latitudeDeltaN2 IN,   ///< Second Latitude delta
    int32 longitudeDeltaN2 IN   ///< Second Longitude delta
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Set number of passengers according to given ecall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SetMsdPassengersCount
(
    Call   ecallRef IN,        ///< SIM slot id
    uint32 passengersCount IN  ///< Passengers count
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Import the PDU MSD according to given ecall reference
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ImportMsd
(
    Call  ecallRef IN,              ///< SIM slot id
    uint8 msd[MAX_MSD_LENGTH] IN    ///< MSD
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Export the PDU MSD according to given ecall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t ExportMsd
(
    Call  ecallRef IN,              ///< SIM slot id
    uint8 msd[MAX_MSD_LENGTH] OUT   ///< MSD output
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Update the eCall MSD in modem to be sent to Public Safety Answering Point
 * (PSAP) when requested.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t SendMsd
(
    Call   ecallRef   IN    ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Start automatic emergency call according to given ecall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_BUSY an eCall session is already in progress
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER bad eCall reference
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t StartAutomatic
(
    Call   ecallRef  IN   ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Start manual emergency call according to given ecall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_BUSY an eCall session is already in progress
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER bad eCall reference
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t StartManual
(
    Call ecallRef IN      ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Initiate a test voice eCall with a configured telephone
 * number stored in the USIM
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_BUSY an eCall session is already in progress
 *      - LE_BAD_PARAMETER bad eCall reference
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t StartTest
(
    Call ecallRef IN      ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Stop the ongoing ecall session according to given ecall reference.
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION le_result_t End
(
    Call ecallRef IN      ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 *  Get currrent eCall state according to given ecall reference
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION State GetState
(
    Call ecallRef IN      ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Get reason for recently terminated call according to given ecall reference
 *
 * @return
 *      - LE_OK on success
 *      - LE_FAULT on failure
 *
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION int32 GetPlatformSpecificTerminationCode
(
    Call ecallRef IN      ///< Emergency call reference
);

//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/**
 * Get termionate reason of recently terminated ecall
 *
 * @return The termination reason.
 *
 * @note If the caller is passing a bad or null pointer into this function, it is a fatal error,
 *         the function may not return.
 */
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FUNCTION TerminationReason GetTerminationReason
(
    Call ecallRef IN        ///< Emergency call reference
);
